#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068460 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc85ca17-8a08-5473-9473-dce954132bd5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Y-Intercept of a Line Given a Point on the Line and Its Slope"}] :question/id #uuid "4ad21d3a-bf40-5b65-8ba6-320d853e6cff" :question/math-academy-id "e-12869" :question/problem "Find the $y$-intercept of the line that passes through the point $(-1, 4)$ and has a slope of $2.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the line passes through the point $(-1,4)$ and its slope is $2$, we substitute $x=-1$, $y=4,$ and $m=2$ into the equation in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\ty &= mx + b \\\n\t(4) &= (2)(-1) + b \\\n\t4 &= -2 + b \\\n\t6 &= b\n}\n$$\n\nSo, the $y$-intercept is $b=6.$ The coordinates of the $y$-intercept are $(0,6).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068461 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e985ae8-05ba-590a-b504-4c84884679f4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points"}] :question/id #uuid "fdc3a6e9-080b-5e2a-b5a4-3af01c7018ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-12870" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the points $(-2,4)$ and $(10,10).$" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ using the given points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}=\\frac{10-4}{10-(-2)}=\\frac{6}{12}=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=\\dfrac 1 2$ into the slope-intercept formula $y=mx+b,$ we reach\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac 1 2 x + b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(10,10)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}x+b \\\\ 10 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10+b \\\\ 10 & =5+b \\\\ b & =10-5 \\\\ b & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is $y=\\dfrac 1 2 x + 5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068462 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068926 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63461668-4f76-52a4-8115-1ab135eef9e3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the X-Intercept of a Line Given a Point and a Slope"}] :question/id #uuid "ec5bebf6-58d8-5b4d-900c-3c024628647c" :question/math-academy-id "e-12871" :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-intercept of the line that passes through the point $(-3,2)$ and has a slope of $-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the line. We know that $m=-\\dfrac{1}{2},$ so we can write the equation of the line as $y=-\\dfrac{1}{2}x + b.$\n\nIt remains to find the $y$-intercept of the line. We can do that by substituting the point $(-3,2)$ into the equation and solving for $b$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+b \\\\ (2) & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-3)+b \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{3}{2}+b \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the line is $y=-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+\\dfrac{1}{2}.$\n\nAt the $x$-intercept, the $y$-coordinate is equal to $0.$ So, we can substitute $y=0$ into the equation and then solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $x=1.$ The coordinates of the $x$-intercept are $(1,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068463 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068927 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f66989ce-aac5-5737-b60b-6ed703634cd5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intercept of a Horizontal or Vertical Line"}] :question/id #uuid "409dfb1f-7400-5539-9dea-6c2d1b6b7ef0" :question/math-academy-id "e-12872" :question/problem "A vertical line $l$ passes through the point $(-6,3).$ Calculate the coordinates of the $x$-intercept of $l.$" :question/worked-solution "On any vertical line, all points have the same $x$-coordinate.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the point $(-6,3)$ is $-6,$ so the $x$-coordinate of the $x$-intercept is also $-6.$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the $x$-intercept are $(-6,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068927 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f66989ce-aac5-5737-b60b-6ed703634cd5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intercept of a Horizontal or Vertical Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7adc1451-d1cd-58a4-84f2-b22398e4e04d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491667} {:answer/id #uuid "98c93e76-7f5a-5b05-a53d-fb9852baf1e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491720} {:answer/id #uuid "b484b0d7-f71b-59d8-a5d1-e45f08ca1f87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491765} {:answer/id #uuid "bd09e13d-3491-5b1f-ab07-7c4595ed9ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no $x$-intercept" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491778} {:answer/id #uuid "d982357e-c293-541d-8d0e-49e2e9734c6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7adc1451-d1cd-58a4-84f2-b22398e4e04d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491667} :answer-field/id #uuid "74663d0d-ac06-549f-8e29-be005604cb7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a49465b-4659-5dd8-a025-f787ff3c780c" :question/math-academy-id "q-109501" :question/problem "A vertical line $l$ passes through the point $(-4,-5).$ Calculate the coordinates of the $x$-intercept of $l.$" :question/worked-solution "On any vertical line, all points have the same $x$-coordinate.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the point $(-4,-5)$ is $-4,$ so the $x$-coordinate of the $x$-intercept is also $-4$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the $x$-intercept are $(-4,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc85ca17-8a08-5473-9473-dce954132bd5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Y-Intercept of a Line Given a Point on the Line and Its Slope"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05ddffe9-4947-5d4a-841c-e28e064e4cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05ddffe9-4947-5d4a-841c-e28e064e4cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491462} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eab90f6-8104-52b0-a6e8-bb42dffbc15f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491938} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be1a0803-b6a6-5853-b14e-c386f57e1c7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be1a0803-b6a6-5853-b14e-c386f57e1c7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491780} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c18f250-6379-5b1b-b0d6-c80a2aaf1a4c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491945}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2c65fb38-ffb7-5f87-a162-80bfea9cae28" :question/math-academy-id "q-177589" :question/problem "Consider the line that has a slope of $\\frac{5}{2}$ and passes through the point $(6,7).$ What are the coordinates of the $y$-intercept?\n\nThe coordinates of the $y$-intercept are\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Given that $m=\\frac{5}{2}$, we substitute the coordinates of the given point into the equation in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =mx+b \\\\ (7) & =(\\frac{5}{2})(6)+b \\\\ 7 & =15+b \\\\ -8 & =b \\\\ b & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the $y$-intercept are $(0,-8).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e985ae8-05ba-590a-b504-4c84884679f4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6356a496-66dd-5026-af4d-1c9be9af7c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6356a496-66dd-5026-af4d-1c9be9af7c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491634} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2bd06f4-cc3d-5c1d-b1ba-721712fb8e26" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e39b88e8-65bf-522f-9eb8-147e26a8aac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e39b88e8-65bf-522f-9eb8-147e26a8aac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491843} :answer-field/id #uuid "d46763ae-93fc-5ef5-adcb-9bf186e709fc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c3bccae-4e28-5fb1-b439-021959c48cae" :question/math-academy-id "q-177611" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b6d0bd3fbb089a811a638b1115a5b5becb6ab9673567c227920ac60b0ec5fbfb.png)\n\nThe equation of the line shown above is $y=${{field-1}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we see that our line passes through the points $(2,1)$ and $(4,4).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ using the given points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-1}{4-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=\\frac{3}{2}$ into the slope-intercept formula $y=mx+b,$ we reach\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3}{2}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{3}{2}x+b \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{3}{2}(2)+b \\\\ 1 & =3+b \\\\ 1-3 & =b \\\\ -2 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is $y=\\frac{3}{2}\\,x-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492040 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e985ae8-05ba-590a-b504-4c84884679f4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7714601-a2ef-59ad-b018-095b5608ac62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7714601-a2ef-59ad-b018-095b5608ac62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491770} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a14d225-1c82-570c-9773-b94607c26c6b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8fbfd4a-aa4b-58f6-afb8-386e88780fcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8fbfd4a-aa4b-58f6-afb8-386e88780fcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491853} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa95a353-245c-575f-8186-845ba9bf2eba" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fe1d449-6681-5500-8e11-aea191ceb681" :question/math-academy-id "q-177619" :question/problem "The equation of the line that passes through the points $(-6,6)$ and $(2,0)$ is $y=${{field-1}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ using the given points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-6}{2-(-6)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=-\\frac{3}{4}$ into the slope-intercept formula $y=mx+b,$ we reach\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{3}{4}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =-\\frac{3}{4}x+b \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{3}{4}(2)+b \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{3}{2}+b \\\\ 0+\\frac{3}{2} & =b \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the equation of the line is $y=-\\frac{3}{4}\\,x+\\frac{3}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068926 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63461668-4f76-52a4-8115-1ab135eef9e3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the X-Intercept of a Line Given a Point and a Slope"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d6a452a-4b7f-5c20-ba5c-ac726ba7c784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491600} {:answer/id #uuid "5f28e5cb-ad57-5f4e-ac1c-91d711e0ba8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491626} {:answer/id #uuid "704be45d-3762-5560-951b-ffb24267fb5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491657} {:answer/id #uuid "9e59fa1a-2907-5c93-a186-2b573b5fcc8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491733} {:answer/id #uuid "9f921f84-7d58-5ec7-a2d4-ebd0686540dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e59fa1a-2907-5c93-a186-2b573b5fcc8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491733} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef92c7c-115a-55f0-91d6-f2cf046dedba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9c4138f5-626e-5679-8f46-0950de2b2243" :question/math-academy-id "q-31571" :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-intercept of the line that passes through the point $(0,6)$ and has a slope of $-2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the line. We know that $m=-2,$ so we can write the equation of the line as $y=-2x+b.$\n\nSince the line passes through the point $(0,6)$, then the $y$-intercept of the line is $b=6.$ \n\nSo, the equation of the line is $y=-2x+6.$\n\nAt the $x$-intercept, the $y$-coordinate is equal to $0.$ So, we can substitute $y=0$ into the equation and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+6 \\\\ 0 & =-2x+6 \\\\ -6 & =-2x \\\\ 3 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $x=3.$ The coordinates of the $x$-intercept are $(3,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068927 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f66989ce-aac5-5737-b60b-6ed703634cd5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intercept of a Horizontal or Vertical Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0412da75-7e9d-5995-8f4e-d3f74d445a60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491457} {:answer/id #uuid "2d6c67b1-1164-5039-a698-994b61affb98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no $y$-intercept" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491546} {:answer/id #uuid "32ce090c-77c1-5d56-a94d-804991e10b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491556} {:answer/id #uuid "51d1b691-b3ae-5945-9544-55a0562241d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491610} {:answer/id #uuid "e41b3323-e442-5057-8ef7-e75373a029a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d6c67b1-1164-5039-a698-994b61affb98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no $y$-intercept" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491546} :answer-field/id #uuid "521160ac-9af5-5d8b-b7c8-e8f8a63187f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "299ed022-6491-500b-9d16-f32033504038" :question/math-academy-id "q-31607" :question/problem "Find the $y$-intercept of the line $x=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "The line $x=-3$ is vertical. So, there is no $y$-intercept.\n\n![](images/06/06464ead0fd419134aeb6eb58d9ca75f7ceff53bb6512b3d9b41b6fcebdd5054.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc85ca17-8a08-5473-9473-dce954132bd5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Y-Intercept of a Line Given a Point on the Line and Its Slope"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14163be2-82b4-5e4d-94d8-e34ff6f47a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491494} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1bef39-ab41-57db-84a4-a5efcb0eea38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491623} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc73bc2-dd0f-5a2c-bc11-e5f9536c648c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491651} {:answer/id #uuid "70d51575-b302-510a-8b46-be8452cd25cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491658} {:answer/id #uuid "94efd0c7-d391-5b80-8bc1-222c2588b844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94efd0c7-d391-5b80-8bc1-222c2588b844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491710} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c6dba06-c9bd-5ba6-bbe8-30a47b79b7c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "48481581-ae0e-5785-8535-25cf6844d8e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-3243" :question/problem "Find the $y$-intercept of the line that passes through the point $(-6,8)$ and has a slope of $\\frac{3}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the line passes through the point $(-6,8)$ and its slope is $\\frac{3}{2}$, we substitute $x=-6$, $y=8,$ and $m=\\frac{3}{2}$ into the equation in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =mx+b \\\\ (8) & =(\\frac{3}{2})(-6)+b \\\\ 8 & =-\\frac{18}{2}+b \\\\ 8 & =-9+b \\\\ 17 & =b \\\\ b & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $y$-intercept is $b=17.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492053 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068926 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63461668-4f76-52a4-8115-1ab135eef9e3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the X-Intercept of a Line Given a Point and a Slope"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01d29151-b1b5-518c-8d19-d8984bede98d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{2},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491451} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd45405-782e-59e0-ac02-1d6083e2e5ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491575} {:answer/id #uuid "97551ddd-3ecb-55ec-980b-daa0290c2219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{4},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491716} {:answer/id #uuid "d215964c-6676-5508-b286-9156a95dff7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{8},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491810} {:answer/id #uuid "e102f780-d3e0-560f-9e57-51aa54dc86f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97551ddd-3ecb-55ec-980b-daa0290c2219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3}{4},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491716} :answer-field/id #uuid "49ec0b4f-a05d-53db-aaed-233499e93db5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4c41a1e-4763-56d9-b8a5-f90945969e38" :question/math-academy-id "q-44385" :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-intercept of the line that passes through the point $(0,\\frac{3}{2})$ and has a slope of $2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the line. We know that $m=2,$ so we can write the equation of the line as $y=2x+b.$\n\nSince the line passes through the point $(0,\\frac{3}{2})$, then the $y$-intercept of the line is $b=\\frac{3}{2}.$ \n\nSo, the equation of the line is $y=2x+\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nAt the $x$-intercept, the $y$-coordinate is equal to $0.$ So, we can substitute $y=0$ into the equation and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & =2x+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & =2x \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $x=-\\frac{3}{4}.$ The coordinates of the $x$-intercept are $(-\\frac{3}{4},0).$"}]}
